// acts chivalrous and noble but it's all fake, frequent drinker, keeps his head high, jealous of his height.
// death not specified — mysterious, unrevealed.
// file: guard, speaker: Guard

// ============================================================
// CASUAL
// ============================================================

title: Guard_Casual_01
tags: casual
speaker: guard
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual01
Guard: [auto/] This stage of the afterlife doesn't seem to have much wine, hopefully the next one does.
//END: casual01
===

title: Guard_Casual_02
tags: casual
speaker: guard
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual02
Guard: [auto/] Between hands is when a disciplined man reflects on strategy. That is what I am doing. Reflecting.
//END: casual02
===

title: Guard_Casual_03
tags: casual
speaker: guard
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual03
Guard: [auto/] They used to call me the Iron Gate of the Eastern Pass. Well, one man called me that. He was also drunk. But it caught on. In a small circle.
//END: casual03
===

title: Guard_Casual_04
tags: casual
speaker: guard
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual04
Guard: [auto/] I have dined at tables far grander than this one.
//END: casual04
===

title: Guard_Casual_05
tags: casual
speaker: guard
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual05
Guard: [auto/] A gentleman never reveals his rank unprompted. But if anyone were to ask, I served in a capacity that was — let us say — adjacent to nobility. Very adjacent.
//END: casual05
===

title: Guard_Casual_06
tags: casual
speaker: guard
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual06
Guard: [auto/] Ah, the pause between hands. In the barracks we called this the Gentleman's Intermission. We did not. I just made that up. But it sounds right, does it not?
//END: casual06
===

title: Guard_Casual_07
tags: casual
speaker: guard
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual07
Guard: [auto/] A man of my experience reads the table like a book. A very complex book. Written in a language I am still learning. But confidently.
//END: casual07
===

title: Guard_Casual_08
tags: casual
speaker: guard
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual08
Guard: [auto/] I sit with excellent posture because it commands respect.
//END: casual08
===

title: Guard_Casual_09
tags: casual
speaker: guard
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual09
Guard: [auto/] Some men play cards for sport. I play for the intellectual contest. And the drinking. Mostly the drinking, if I am being — no. The intellectual contest.
//END: casual09
===

title: Guard_Casual_10
tags: casual
speaker: guard
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual10
Guard: [auto/] Is this seat lower than the others? It feels lower. I demand — I request, humbly, that someone inspect the legs of this chair.
//END: casual10
===

title: Guard_Casual_11
tags: casual
speaker: guard
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual11
Guard: [auto/] The art of the bluff is really about conviction. You must believe the lie yourself. That is... general card advice. Not a confession.
//END: casual11
===

title: Guard_Casual_12
tags: casual
speaker: guard
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual12
Guard: [auto/] I keep my chin high because it projects authority. A man who looks down is a man who has already surrendered. Also I appear taller but that's beside the point.
//END: casual12
===

title: Guard_Casual_13
tags: casual
speaker: guard
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual13
Guard: [auto/] I once told a woman I was a decorated captain. She asked which regiment. I said it was classified. She said classified regiments do not drink rice wine from a bucket. The evening ended shortly after.
//END: casual13
===

title: Guard_Casual_14
tags: casual
speaker: guard
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual14
Guard: [auto/] Do you know the worst part of the afterlife? No one here is impressed by rank anymore. You could say you commanded ten thousand men and the ghost next to you can say twenty, no one actually remembers the numbers though.
//END: casual14
===

title: Guard_Casual_15
tags: casual
speaker: guard
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual15
Guard: [auto/] I drink to remember the version of myself I tell people about. He was taller, braver, invited to things. Good man.
//END: casual15
===

title: Guard_Casual_16
tags: casual
speaker: guard
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual16
Guard: [auto/] Some nights I cannot sleep — can spirits sleep? Regardless. Some nights I lie awake and wonder if anyone ever actually believed me.
//END: casual16
===

